An Azure landing zone provides a standardized foundation for deploying and managing workloads in Azure. Its architecture is designed to establish common capabilities before individual application teams begin building their solutions.

Important landing zone components include:

* Management groups
* Subscriptions
* Microsoft Entra ID
* Azure RBAC
* Networking
* Security controls
* Azure Policy
* Monitoring and management
* Resource organization

For example, an enterprise may establish centralized identity, networking, and governance capabilities while giving application teams separate subscriptions for their workloads.

A real-life use case is a large organization migrating multiple business applications to Azure and using a common landing-zone architecture to ensure every workload follows the same foundational standards.

Landing zones reduce duplicated effort and provide a consistent starting point for enterprise cloud adoption.
